      "description": "Watch Anderlecht vs PAOK highlights and goals from UEFA Europa League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 13, 2026. On August 13, 2026 , the UEFA Europa League delivered a captivating spectacle as Anderlecht hosted PAOK in a clash filled with tactical shifts. Both sides pushed for dominance in a game that remained unpredictable until the final whistle. First Half Deadlock Broken The match began with high intensity as both teams looked to establish early rhythm. Anderlecht broke the deadlock in the 19th minute when Leo Petrot found the back of the net, thanks to a well-placed assist from Giulian Biancone . However, the lead was short-lived. PAOK responded with determination, and in the 34th minute, Andrija Zivkovic finished clinically to level the score after a precise pass from Christos Zafeiris . The teams went into the break with everything to play for. Anderlecht's Second Half Surge The home side came out of the tunnel with renewed energy, taking control of the match immediately. Just two minutes into the second half, in the 47th minute, Lukas Ambros restored Anderlecht 's lead, with Giulian Biancone providing his second assist of the night. The pressure didn't stop there. In the 55th minute, Danylo Sikan capitalized on a ball from Mihajlo Cvetkovic to make it 3-1, putting the Belgian side in a commanding position. Late Penalty and Red Card Chaos As the clock ticked down, the atmosphere grew increasingly tense. PAOK were thrown a lifeline in the 88th minute when they were awarded a penalty, which Alexander Jeremejeff converted with composure. However, the comeback attempt quickly unraveled. Andrija Zivkovic was shown a straight red card in the 89th minute, followed by Alexander Jeremejeff receiving his marching orders in the 93rd minute amidst heavy protests. Despite a late yellow card for Nathan Saliba , Anderlecht secured the 3-2 victory in a frantic finish."
